\title{shinygazer: Interactive Pupil Pre-Processing with 'gazeR'}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A 'shiny' app for pre-processing pupillometry data without writing code, built on the 'gazeR' package. Reads EyeLink .asc files, SR Research Data Viewer sample reports, Tobii (Titta) and Pupil Labs Neon exports; removes blinks (tracker events or noise-based detection) and artifacts; interpolates, smooths, baseline-corrects and time-locks trials; reports data quality and behavioural exclusions; and plots time courses with within- or between-subject error, rainclouds and pupil-behaviour relationships. Every setting is exported so the pipeline can be reproduced.
